=== PARITY NOTES (web Pressure.tsx → native Pressure) ===
  • SI carrier: web fills `sourceBar` which, despite the legacy name, holds kPa (SI.pressure='kPa'):
      bar*100 (kPa per bar) or psi*6.894757 (kPa per psi). Native carries the same kPa in
      PressureSource.kpa (mirrors Distance carrying metres in DistanceSource.meters).
  • Conversion: convertPressureFromSI(kPa→kPa | /6.894757 psi | /100 bar); unknown unit → bar (web
      derivePressure default for a non-psi preference). Factors unit-tested.
  • Precedence: bar checked first (when finite), then psi (web `if (bar…) else if (psi…)`).
  • fmtNumber parity: half-away-from-zero rounding + locale grouping (en_US vs de_DE), precision
      precedence prop→preference→2 clamped 0...20, "en-US" locale fallback, toFixed(2) tooltip.
  • Empty sentinel "—" when neither input is finite (web `sourceBar == null`).
  • i18n: web renders no translatable copy; the unit label is the user's `unitPrefs.pressure` symbol and
      the number is locale-formatted. The lone catalog key is the native empty-state VoiceOver label
      "pressure.empty.accessibilityLabel" (Pressure.strings) — a refinement over the web bare "—".
  • States: the web source is a synchronous formatter (props + the synchronous useUnits() preference bag,
      no fetch) → no loading/error/stale/offline axis exists to reproduce. The genuine branches the web
      has — value (figure + unit + tooltip) and empty ("—") — are both reproduced and tested. Same
      disposition as the sibling 0085 Distance / 0075 AnimatedNumber surfaces.

